$DIR/main.p:17:25: o was moved into consume (its parameter takes a Buf by value) at line 18, but the deferred function (line 17) uses it when the function returns
    Buf is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it when they
    are dropped. Passing an owner by value moves it instead of copying it, so
    that what it owns has exactly one owner. Since line 18, o holds nothing. The
    function literal deferred at line 17 runs when the function returns, after
    line 18, so it would use what o no longer holds.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    Give o a new value after line 18, so that the deferred function finds one:
        o = Buf{}
    Or do the work of the deferred function at the end of the function, before
    line 18, instead of deferring it
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3301" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/main.p:23:25: o may have been moved into consume (its parameter takes a Buf by value) at line 25, but the deferred function (line 23) uses it when the function returns
    Buf is an owner type: its values own what they hold and release it when they
    are dropped. o is moved into consume (its parameter takes a Buf by value) at
    line 25 on some paths to this point and not on others. On those paths o
    holds nothing afterwards, and the compiler cannot let a value be used where
    it may already belong to someone else. The function literal deferred at line
    23 runs when the function returns, after line 25, so it would use what o no
    longer holds.
    Go copies such values freely and its garbage collector frees what they refer
    to when nothing refers to it any more. Plutonium has no garbage collector:
    an owner frees what it owns when it is dropped, so there must be exactly
    one.
    Give o a new value after line 25, so that the deferred function finds one:
        o = Buf{}
    Or do the work of the deferred function at the end of the function, before
    line 25, instead of deferring it
    (see "Moves" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.5)
    (run "pluto explain E3302" for a longer explanation)
